# .vercelignore
# ---------------
# Controls what gets UPLOADED to Vercel's build servers (vercel.json's
# functions.excludeFiles only trims the post-build FUNCTION bundle, not the
# upload — found the hard way: an 808MB initial upload and a 1.4GB reported
# bundle size for a project whose actual Python source is only a few MB,
# because this file didn't exist and the local venv/ (which accumulates
# dev-only packages like gradio/playwright/faiss over time — see
# requirements-local.txt) was being uploaded wholesale.

venv/
.venv/
env/
ENV/
**/venv/
**/.venv/

.git/
.github/

data/
output/
rag_data/
vector_storage/
test/_tmp/

docs/
design/
review/
turtle_vault/
.obsidian/

node_modules/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
__pycache__/
**/__pycache__/
*.pyc

.env
.env.*
!.env.example
.env.local

*.log
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3
*.db
